    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0484" n="474" xml:id="pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/971a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-24T22:00:00-04:00">November 24,
                            1943—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1690. For Adler from the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Mr. Hsi Te-mou and Mr. T. L. Soong have informed the Treasury that Dr.
                        Kung agrees with the Treasury that under present circumstances the 1941
                        Agreement should not be renewed.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The Treasury herewith instructs you to submit your resignation to Dr. Kung
                        as of December 31, although at your discretion you may postpone date of
                        resignation until January 31, 1944, if you feel that additional month may be
                        necessary to wind up Board’s affairs. [Morgenthau.]</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
